-- title:
--   Distinct minimal primes over q and 1/j generate the unit ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime. Write $F$ for the subfield of the field of Laurent series over $\mathbf{Q}$ generated over $\mathbf{Q}$ by the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbf{Q}\ d\ j_q$ for the divisors $d$ of $q$, let $j \in F$ denote the element `IgusaScheme.jFull q` (the series $j_q$ viewed in $F$), and let $A =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf ℤ F j` be the subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements of $F$ integral over the subring $\mathbf{Z}[j^{-1}]$ generated by $j^{-1}$, that is, the integral closure of $\mathbf{Z}[1/j]$ in $F$. Let $\mathfrak{q}$ and $\mathfrak{q}'$ be two ideals of $A$, each a minimal prime over the principal ideal generated by the image of $q$ in $A$, and assume $\mathfrak{q} \neq \mathfrak{q}'$. Then
--   $$\mathfrak{q} + \mathfrak{q}' + (j^{-1})\,A = A,$$
--   where $j^{-1}$ denotes the element `TwoChartIntegralModel.jInvChartInf ℤ F j` of $A$ and the sum is the supremum of the three ideals in the lattice of ideals of $A$.
--
--   In the two-chart integral model of the modular curve at level $q$, the ring $A$ is the coordinate ring of the chart around the cusps (where $j$ has a pole), and the minimal primes over $(q)$ correspond to the irreducible components of the fibre at $q$. The statement says that two distinct such components do not meet on the locus $j^{-1} = 0$, i.e. the two cusps reduce onto different components; it is used in the corresponding assertion for the Igusa scheme at a level prime to the residue characteristic.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModel_sup_sup_span_jInvChartInf_eq_top_of_mem_minimalPrimes.lean

